[h1]R.A.T.S. Sensor Views[/h1]
[i]R.A.T.S. – Reconnaissance, Acoustics, Terrain & Signals[/i]

[b]Sit down, Commander. Your cruiser has a real radar room now.[/b]
See who sees what: a green phosphor radar scope, a sonar waterfall, a sensor board and live sensor lines on your tactical map. Everything opens from one radar button at the bottom right.

[h2]The highlights[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]A radar that looks like one.[/b] Green phosphor tube, the sweep leaves a glowing trail, contacts light up when it hits them and fade until the next pass
[*][b]Sonar with depth.[/b] Waterfall with baffle sectors, your own noise and a depth strip with thermal layer and seabed
[*][b]Know where you are blind.[/b] Coverage on the map shows where your radar goes dark behind hills
[*][b]Click and fly.[/b] Click a contact on the scope and the camera flies to it. Click your own ships too
[*][b]Everything on one button.[/b] One flyout opens every window and flips every map layer
[/list]

[h2]Radar scope[/h2]
[list]
[*]Only what your radar really holds, fading until the next pass of the sweep; nothing while the radar is off
[*]Range changes glide instead of jumping
[*]Radar horizon ring: set the target altitude with the slider or type it in
[*]Blind arcs of your search radars
[*]Your own ships under the same rule, strobes for radars warning you and for jammers
[*]A LOCK ring on contacts held by a fire-control radar
[*]North-up or heading-up, and a measuring cursor with bearing and range
[/list]

[h2]Sonar display[/h2]
[list]
[*]Bearing over time, newest at the top, for the sonar you pick
[*]Baffle sector shaded, your own noise at your speed shown
[*]Depth strip: thermal layer, your depth, the array, the seabed and the contacts at the depth the game estimates
[*]Echoes button: switch the waterfall to a bearing and range plot
[/list]

[h2]Sensor board[/h2]
[list]
[*]Your units across, the contacts down, and which sensor holds what: R search radar, F fire control, E ESM, S passive sonar, A active sonar, V visual or infrared, M MAD
[*]Click a cell for bearing, range and age per sensor. Double-click a contact to bring the camera to it
[*]The selected unit's sensors with on or off, damage, arcs and EMCON
[/list]

[h2]On the map[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Sensor lines:[/b] a line from each of your units to where each sensor puts a contact. Amber for search radar, thick red for a fire-control lock, blue for active sonar, dotted for visual, a wedge for ESM and passive sonar
[*][b]Coverage:[/b] where the selected unit's sensors would hold an imagined target. Radar with terrain shadows, ESM, visual range and passive sonar. Off by default
[*]Lines for the selected unit or for all of your units, per sensor type
[/list]

[h2]Open it[/h2]
[list]
[*]One radar button at the right end of the bottom bar opens the flyout: Board, Radar scope and Sonar (each one alone) plus the map switches
[*]Hot keys: Ctrl+Insert, Ctrl+PageUp, Ctrl+PageDown for the windows, Ctrl+Shift+PageUp and Ctrl+Shift+PageDown for the map layers. All can be changed in the config
[*]With [b]R.A.T.S. Pop-Out Windows[/b] the windows can go to a second monitor
[/list]

[h2]Good to know[/h2]
[list]
[*]Display only. It shows what your own sensors already report to the game's plotting table. The real position of a contact is never shown, and nothing in a mission changes: the mission's own rules decide what a sensor can detect
[*]Passive sonar depth is the game's own rough estimate and can be off by hundreds of feet
[*]No game files are changed. If a game update moves something the mod hooks into, the log says what turned off
[/list]

[h2]Install[/h2]
[b]R.A.T.S. Keel[/b] is required: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3835527459]subscribe[/url] and switch it on in the Mods menu; its page has the one install step. It replaces Anchor Chain.
Run in the game on the 3D globe public beta (build 261107). The build for 0.8.7 passes the offline checks; the right DLL loads on each game and the other stays off.

[h2]Problems?[/h2]
For a bug, attach [i]<Sea Power>\BepInEx\LogOutput.log[/i] (as a link) and say which window and which unit. Settings are in [i]BepInEx\config\dev.sewerlabs.seapowersensorviews.cfg[/i].

Source code (MIT): [url=https://github.com/struckl/SeaPowerSensorViews]github.com/struckl/SeaPowerSensorViews[/url]

[i]R.A.T.S. – Ratte's Assorted Tactical Systems[/i]
